 incorporated. Their technique recognized behaviors of lane-keeping, lanechanging, and distracted driving. In [8], the IMM was applied to estimate a vehicle’s intent at an intersection. In [7] and [13], the IMM is used for state and maneuver estimation as well as prediction. The curvi-linear coordinate system (CCS) is applied to constrain the motion of the vehicle to within road boundaries. The IMM tracking and behavior estimation technique in [11] performs trajectory prediction as described above, but only for straight-line and turning maneuvers. In [14] and [15], a modified IMM algorithm is used for prediction only. It relied on physics and maneuver-based models to predict trajectories. In [16], the IMM-KF was utilized to find the most probable maneuver using new intention-based motion
