B. Trajectory Prediction Based on IMM-GVBL-SVSF
The objective of this component is to predict the path of a tracked vehicle up to tp seconds ahead of the current time. The goal in other words is to predict the trajectory of the vehicle up to N p time steps ahead of the current time step k. Each iteration of prediction works similarly to each cycle of an IMM estimator. The difference is that the mode and mixing probabilities from the current time tk are retained as being constant for prediction given that there are no measurements available from the future time steps. Also, in mode-matched filtering, only the prediction stage executes due to no measurement again being available from the future. The current mode-conditioned state estimates, co-variances,
