V. SIMULATION AND EXPERIMENTAL RESULTS
The performance of the proposed approach is evaluated using synthetically generated data as well as measured and real data from two public real data-sets. The IMM-GVBL-SVSF and IMM-KF are comparatively analyzed in terms of trajectory prediction performance. They are also compared to some stateof-the-art machine learning approaches. Section V-A gives a description of the performance metrics used, section V-B shows the results with simulated data, and section V-C has the experimental results from two real data-sets that compare IMM-KF and IMM-GVBL-SVSF only. Section V-D gives a qualitative comparison of the IMM methods. Section V-E has a comparison with machine learning methods on the same experimental data-sets. Lastly, section V-F discusses limitations of the proposed approach. Note that two real data-sets were mainly used for the purpose of comparing the IMM strategies to data-driven approaches. In works that use explicit closed-form mathematical models to predict trajectories, it is common to use only one real data-set and/or synthetic data.
