F. Limitations of Proposed Approach
A limitation of the proposed approach as well as IMM-KF is that both algorithms are sensitive to the noise variance of the measurements. This is evident by the comparative results from the application of IMM strategies on the low noise HighD data-set compared to the high noise NGSIM data-set. In terms of the latency in detecting the maneuvers, this is also present with real data. As an example, from one vehicle in the HighD data-set, the vehicle’s lateral position is shown in Figure 16, based on that the lane-change begins at approximately 2s. Figure 17 shows the maneuver probability of the VT-LC model for the upper adjacent lane when using IMM-GVBL-SVSF, as shown, the probability is first above 0.8 at 3.12s, thus, the latency in recognizing the lane-change is about 1.12s. In the VT-LC model for the upper adjacent lane, the central lateral position of that lane is set as the reference lateral
