Layer- Smooth Variable Structure Filter (IMM-GVBL-SVSF), where the estimated states and maneuver probabilities were utilized to predict lane-changing and lane-keeping trajectories. Motion models defined in the CCS that account for the road geometry constraints were selected to represent the lane-changing and lane-keeping maneuvers. A highway scenario was also assumed. The main contribution of the study is the comparative analysis of the IMM-KF and IMMGVBL-SVSF for trajectory prediction in simulated and real driving scenarios. In the absence of uncertainties in the simulated scenarios, the IMM-KF performs better. When modeling uncertainties are added, the IMM-GVBL-SVSF outperforms the IMM-KF strategy in terms of its performance, robustness and stability. This is because the GVBL-SVSF’s switching gain is based on the sliding mode concept and provides better robustness and stability with respect to uncertainties. In simulated cases, the IMM-KF’s performance degrades considerably as uncertainties are increased; its RMSE becomes larger than 1m and it becomes unstable. In contrast, the IMMGVBL-SVSF is robust and provides a reasonable prediction by remaining stable and detecting mode changes early in maneuvers. In terms of experimental results, IMM-GVBLSVSF performs better. In majority of the cases it outperforms IMM-KF due to robustness to non-Gaussian modelling errors, which also allows lane-changes to be recognized earlier. Moreover, the proposed approach and IMM-KF were compared to learning-based strategies to get an idea of what the performance gap is between data-driven methods. It was found that on a low noise data-set if the position and longitudinal velocity of the remote vehicles are measurements, the IMM-GVBL-SVSF provides comparable performance to learning-based approaches without requiring training data. As future work, the IMM approach may be augmented with AI strategies to improve prediction performance. A possibility is to represent maneuvers using machine learning models instead of hand-crafted models because a limitation associated with hand-crafted models is that the model may not represent future motion accurately.
